script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'analyzer-edit-forensics',
  description: 'Forensic investigation: which pipeline stage changed the shipped interop analyzer, when, under what authority, and what each adversary panel said about it.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Investigate', detail: 'three independent lenses: stage authority, forensic timeline, adversary verdicts' },
    { title: 'Synthesize', detail: 'reconcile into one timeline and an authority ruling', model: 'opus' },
  ],
}

const PROJECT = '/Users/timothystockstill/code/macos/4thWAIV/agent-guard'
const SESSIONS = '/Users/timothystockstill/.claude/projects/-Users-timothystockstill-code-macos-4thWAIV-agent-guard'
const CONTRACT = PROJECT + '/.dev/inprocess/2026-08-23-os-presence-check/contract-linux-policy-path.md'

const FACTS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  additionalProperties: false,
  properties: {
    lensId: { type: 'string' },
    facts: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        additionalProperties: false,
        properties: {
          claim: { type: 'string' },
          evidence: { type: 'string' },
          confidence: { type: 'string', enum: ['proven', 'likely', 'unknown'] },
        },
        required: ['claim', 'evidence', 'confidence'],
      },
    },
    unanswered: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
  required: ['lensId', 'facts'],
}

const SUBJECT = `THE SUBJECT OF THE INVESTIGATION:
Two files under analyzers/ in ${PROJECT}:
  (a) analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers/InteropOnlyInCrossPlatformLibrariesAnalyzer.cs  — an OLD, already-shipped rule (AG0008) banning [DllImport]/[LibraryImport] outside the per-OS libraries. It was MODIFIED: its AnalyzeAttribute body was replaced by a one-line call to a new shared helper.
  (b) analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers/AppliedAttributeBan.cs — a NEW file holding the extracted shared match-then-report body, now called by BOTH the old AG0008 rule and the new AG0039 [CallerFilePath] rule created by this run.

The governing contract is ${CONTRACT}. Its rule-phase-ruleset section authorizes Rule 1 (a NEW [CallerFilePath] ban analyzer) and Rule 2 (adding "baseDirectory" to an existing rule's parameter list). It does not name AG0008.

The question the human needs answered precisely: WHICH STAGE made this change, WHEN, and was that stage ACTING WITHIN ITS DEFINED AUTHORITY? Do not assume it was a violation and do not assume it was authorized. Find the evidence.`

const LENSES = [
  {
    id: 'stage-authority',
    focus: `Determine what the RULE-PHASE stage is DEFINED to be allowed to do, and whether extracting a shared helper out of an existing shipped analyzer falls inside or outside that authority.
READ IN FULL: ${PROJECT}/.agents/skills/rails-run-a-workflow/SKILL.md (the RULE-PHASE stage definition, the roles list, the rule-gen agent's authority, the cleanup law, separation of powers), ${PROJECT}/.agents/workflows/rule-phase.js (the ACTUAL prompt text given to the rule-gen agent and to its adversary panel — quote the relevant instruction lines verbatim), ${PROJECT}/.agents/skills/rails-read-me/SKILL.md (the "Guard-protected-later areas" section on analyzers/** being decision-gated, and the Rule-Driven Development section), ${PROJECT}/.agents/skills/rails-dry-code/SKILL.md (whether a DRY finding OBLIGATES collapsing duplicate copies into one owner), and the contract ${CONTRACT}.
Answer precisely: (1) Does the rule-gen agent's charter permit editing an EXISTING shipped analyzer, or only writing the new rules the contract names? Quote the text. (2) Does the DRY rail REQUIRE collapsing two copies into one owner when duplication is found, and does that requirement reach an existing analyzer? Quote it. (3) Is there a conflict between "analyzers/** is decision-gated" and "the DRY adversary FAILs duplication"? Quote both. (4) Under the written process, was this extraction the CORRECT move, a violation, or a genuine gap in the process?`,
  },
  {
    id: 'timeline',
    focus: `Establish the forensic TIMELINE: exactly when each of the two files was created/modified, by which pipeline run, and what else changed at the same moment.
Use: filesystem timestamps (ls -la --time-style=full-iso or stat on the two analyzer files AND on every other changed file in git status, so you can cluster them by time), git log/git status/git diff in ${PROJECT}, and the session transcript directory ${SESSIONS} — it contains per-session .jsonl transcripts and a subagents/workflows/ folder with one directory per workflow run, each holding journal.jsonl (one result line per completed agent) plus per-agent .jsonl files. Search those workflow run directories for the RULE-PHASE run: grep for AppliedAttributeBan, InteropOnlyInCrossPlatformLibraries, AG0039, NoCallerFilePath, and rule-gen across ${SESSIONS} to find which run produced these files and when.
Answer precisely: (1) On what date/time were AppliedAttributeBan.cs and the AG0008 modification written? (2) Which workflow run (name + run id + directory) produced them? (3) Which stage was that run — RULE-PHASE, ARCHITECTURE, TDD, or IMPLEMENT? (4) Cluster ALL currently-uncommitted files by modification time and say which stage produced each cluster. (5) Confirm or refute: the IMPLEMENT run (run id wf_7caa18b6-bb9) did NOT touch any file under analyzers/.`,
  },
  {
    id: 'adversary-verdicts',
    focus: `Find out what EVERY adversary panel actually said about the AG0008 edit and the new shared helper, at every stage it was reviewed.
Search ${SESSIONS} — the per-session .jsonl transcripts and every subagents/workflows/*/journal.jsonl and per-agent .jsonl — for the RULE-PHASE run's adversary verdicts (lenses: solid, dry, lie-catcher) and quote what they said about AppliedAttributeBan / the AG0008 refactor. Then compare against the REFUTE run (run id wf_fdafb6b7-37d, whose output is also at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-timothystockstill-code-macos-4thWAIV-agent-guard/bb98df78-31bd-4682-ab83-c3ce54b775b0/tasks/wfo8oz21y.output) where the lie-catcher recorded a finding calling the AG0008 rewrite an unauthorized scope expansion and yet returned verdict PASS.
Answer precisely: (1) Did the RULE-PHASE adversary panel see and approve the AG0008 extraction? Quote them. (2) Did any RULE-PHASE adversary DEMAND the extraction (a DRY finding)? Quote it. (3) Quote the REFUTE lie-catcher's finding text verbatim and its verdict field. (4) Is the REFUTE lie-catcher's PASS-with-a-confirmed-finding consistent with its own instructions in ${PROJECT}/.agents/workflows/refute.js and rails-decisions? Quote the instruction. (5) Do the two panels CONTRADICT each other on the same change?`,
  },
]

const huntPrompt = (lens) => `You are a forensic investigator on ONE lens. Establish FACTS with evidence, not opinions. Quote text verbatim where the question asks for a quote. If you cannot establish something, say so in unanswered rather than guessing.

${SUBJECT}

YOUR LENS — ${lens.id}:
${lens.focus}

Return lensId="${lens.id}", facts (each a claim with its evidence — file:line, a verbatim quote, a command and its output, or a timestamp — and a confidence of proven/likely/unknown), and unanswered (anything you could not establish).`

const found = (await parallel(LENSES.map((lens) => () =>
  agent(huntPrompt(lens), { label: `investigate:${lens.id}`, phase: 'Investigate', schema: FACTS_SCHEMA }))
)).filter(Boolean)

log(`three lenses returned ${found.reduce((n, f) => n + (f.facts || []).length, 0)} facts; synthesizing the timeline and the authority ruling`)

const SYNTH_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  additionalProperties: false,
  properties: {
    timeline: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        additionalProperties: false,
        properties: {
          when: { type: 'string' },
          stage: { type: 'string' },
          whatChanged: { type: 'string' },
          evidence: { type: 'string' },
        },
        required: ['when', 'stage', 'whatChanged'],
      },
    },
    authorityRuling: { type: 'string' },
    wasItAViolation: { type: 'string', enum: ['authorized', 'violation', 'process-gap'] },
    rulingBasis: { type: 'string' },
    adversaryContradiction: { type: 'string' },
    openForTim: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    unresolved: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
  required: ['timeline', 'authorityRuling', 'wasItAViolation', 'rulingBasis'],
}

const synth = await agent(`You are synthesizing a forensic report for a human who has been given three WRONG accounts of this already and is furious about imprecision. Reconcile the three lenses' facts into ONE account. Do not hedge and do not pad. Where the lenses disagree, say which evidence wins and why.

${SUBJECT}

LENS FACTS (JSON):
${JSON.stringify(found, null, 2)}

Produce: timeline (each entry: when, which STAGE, what changed, evidence) covering every uncommitted change in the working tree, not just the analyzer ones; authorityRuling (a plain-English ruling on whether the rule-writing stage was entitled to refactor an existing shipped analyzer, citing the governing text); wasItAViolation (authorized | violation | process-gap); rulingBasis (the quoted text the ruling rests on); adversaryContradiction (whether the RULE-PHASE panel and the REFUTE lie-catcher contradict each other on this same change, and which is right); openForTim (the decisions genuinely left for the human); unresolved (anything the evidence could not settle).`, { label: 'synthesize', phase: 'Synthesize', model: 'opus', schema: SYNTH_SCHEMA })

return { lenses: found, synthesis: synth }
